The Nautilus DevOps team needs to copy data from the jump host to all application servers in Stratos DC using Ansible. Execute the task with the following details:
a. Create an inventory file /home/thor/ansible/inventory on jump_host and add all application servers as managed nodes.
b. Create a playbook /home/thor/ansible/playbook.yml on the jump host to copy the /usr/src/dba/index.html file to all application servers, placing it at /opt/dba.

Note: Validation will run the playbook using the command ansible-playbook -i inventory playbook.yml. Ensure the playbook functions properly without any extra arguments.

SOLUTION
Yes. Since validation runs from /home/thor/ansible with no extra variables, make the inventory self-contained with the SSH credentials already used for these Nautilus servers.

1. Create the inventory

On the jump host:

mkdir -p /home/thor/ansible
cd /home/thor/ansible
nano inventory

Add:

[app]
stapp01 ansible_host=stapp01 ansible_user=tony ansible_ssh_pass=Ir0nM@n
stapp02 ansible_host=stapp02 ansible_user=tony ansible_ssh_pass=Ir0nM@n
stapp03 ansible_host=stapp03 ansible_user=tony ansible_ssh_pass=Ir0nM@n

If your lab's actual SSH password/user differs, use the credentials that successfully worked for your servers.

2. Create the playbook
nano /home/thor/ansible/playbook.yml

Use:

---
- name: Copy DBA index file to all application servers
  hosts: app
  become: true

  tasks:
    - name: Ensure /opt/dba directory exists
      ansible.builtin.file:
        path: /opt/dba
        state: directory
        mode: '0755'

    - name: Copy index.html to application servers
      ansible.builtin.copy:
        src: /usr/src/dba/index.html
        dest: /opt/dba/index.html
        mode: '0644'

Important: src is on the jump host, because copy transfers the file from the Ansible controller to the managed nodes.

3. Test exactly as the validator will
cd /home/thor/ansible
ansible-playbook -i inventory playbook.yml

Then verify:

ansible -i inventory app -m shell -a 'ls -l /opt/dba/index.html'

You should see /opt/dba/index.html on stapp01, stapp02, and stapp03.

If the password you previously used is still the one for tony, the above should run without requiring any extra arguments.
